# .mailmap — one identity for display, without touching a single commit
#
# Owner order OA-dc47a6f71c, 2026-09-13, verbatim: "Form B, Zielidentitaet b7n0de
# <kontakt@b7n0de.com>, kein Realname in der Datei, alle alten Adressen und kraxo@b7n0de.com nur
# ueber die Adresse dorthin abbilden, crissi.jane damit vollstaendig abgebildet."
#
# WHY NO REWRITE (order OA-517479ff38, verbatim): history is not rewritten because tags, receipts,
# provenance and archives are bound to the object names. A .mailmap only changes what `git log`,
# `git shortlog` and `git blame` DISPLAY. Every commit stays byte for byte as it is, and every
# signature, digest and anchoring keeps its validity.
#
# WHY BY ADDRESS AND NOT BY NAME. Mapping by name plus address would keep the owner's real name in
# this file, which the order rules out. Mapping by address alone carries one accepted consequence,
# and the order names it: the entry that wrote under `raponchen@me.com` with a different display
# name is folded in as well. That is a decision, not an oversight.
#
# MEASURED over origin/main, 1139 commits, before this file existed:
#   662  kraxo@b7n0de.com                              173  45888075+b7n0de@users.noreply.github.com
#   132  support@zudiroderzumir.de                      99  kontakt@b7n0de.com
#    28  raponchen@me.com                               17  b7n0de@users.noreply.github.com
#     3  security@b7n0de.com
#   plus dependabot, one outside contribution and one foreign account, none of them this owner.
#
# THE IDENTITY BOUNDARY, for the register, CORRECTED after Codex round one measured it against the
# graph rather than against the dates. The earlier wording claimed that
# d4558036a04032a3747d9f72de7213e9d5c34dcb of 2026-09-07T12:52:11+02:00 is "the first point after
# which no older address follows", with 117 commits behind it. Both numbers were wrong, and the
# error is worth naming because it is a whole class: the sentence is a statement about the DAG, and
# it was derived from a list sorted by DATE.
#
# Measured at a7510d2: d4558036 has 128 descendants, not 117, and FOUR of them carry
# support@zudiroderzumir.de — 25c23fa3, cebbdf9d, 167eba39, f023a590, authored on 2026-09-07 between
# 06:57 and 08:12, therefore EARLIER than d4558036 by the clock and LATER than it in the graph,
# because they were integrated afterwards. `git log A..B` answers a question about reachability; a
# date answers a different one.
#
# What holds, stated separately because the two orders disagree:
#   by DATE   the last commit carrying an older address is b9d35d492db87267ae197d882126c12fea9eeb14
#             of 2026-09-07T12:15:53+02:00. That half of the earlier sentence was correct.
#   by GRAPH  the first point after which no older address follows is
#             7616293c247be82063603955e76770e6849ad781 of 2026-09-13T11:17:04+02:00, with exactly
#             two descendants, both of them this identity work. It sits that late because the merge
#             at that commit brought in a whole branch whose commits are topologically after every
#             earlier candidate while carrying older addresses: the candidate one step older,
#             3dfea31e, still has 80 of them behind it.
#   by SCOPE at b96b961e1c6bd40b40c7139925564d08a3e0e22f the branch carries 1163 commits. 779 were
#             authored under one of the two house addresses, so 384 were not. Of those 384, twenty
#             four are third party and not this owner at all, twenty from Dependabot, three from an
#             outside contributor and one from a foreign account. That leaves 360 authored under an
#             older address OF THIS OWNER.
#
#             The earlier line gave a single number, 376, and called all of it older addresses of
#             this owner. It was the complement of the two house addresses, and a complement is not
#             a membership test. Everything that is not us was counted as an older us, which put
#             twenty two third party commits inside this identity. The fix is the separation, not a
#             smaller number.
#
#             Reproduce with `git log <head> --no-use-mailmap --format='%ae' | sort | uniq -c`. Each
#             count names the head it was measured at, because a count without one cannot be checked
#             and goes stale in silence.
#
# The house identity first appears in d602802c5bb3daeb76439c99651d84220a894306 of 2026-07-09 and
# does not hold from there. None of this rewrites anything: the mapping below normalises the
# DISPLAY, and every commit keeps the sha its receipts, tags and provenance are bound to.

# Die ZIELADRESSE braucht eine eigene Zeile, und das ist nicht Zierde. GEMESSEN ohne sie:
# 101 Commits, die kontakt@b7n0de.com bereits benutzten, blieben unter ihren alten
# Anzeigenamen stehen, darunter zweimal der Realname. Eine Abbildung ueber die Adresse
# normalisiert den NAMEN einer Adresse nur, wenn die Adresse selbst eine Zeile hat.
b7n0de <kontakt@b7n0de.com> <kontakt@b7n0de.com>
b7n0de <kontakt@b7n0de.com> <kraxo@b7n0de.com>
b7n0de <kontakt@b7n0de.com> <support@zudiroderzumir.de>
